"Imagination VP David Harold will explain how, having built its success on the back of mobile, Imagination is looking at the next big challenges for IP innovation: the widely different segments we tend to lump together as AI. Can they be addressed as one opportunity or are there too many different challenges? Where does AI intersect with established markets like automotive, surveillance and consumer or parallel opportunities like IoT? And at the heart of this: what does a solution for mass market AI really look like?\nDiscover what opportunities there are for devices and applications targeted at markets that will be impacted by AI.\nFind out about the benefits of edge neural network acceleration, and key tech features like variable precision.\nAsk questions about overall technology strategy from Imagination in this area.\nAs Vice President of Marketing and Communications at Imagination, David Harold is responsible for partnerships, branding and marketing. David joined Imagination to lead its PR efforts in 1998, and during that time was also Director of PR for PURE Digital, a consumer brand of Imagination. Before that, he held PR management roles at VideoLogic, Cohn & Wolfe and SMI. He holds a BA in English Literature and Film Studies and an MA in Creative Writing from University of East Anglia, Norwich, UK."
