"PlayaEvents : 2009 Event \u2014 Black Rock Solar- talk to us!\nBlack Rock Solar- talk to us!\nBlack Rock Solar is committed to creating, implementing and demonstrating a sustainable model for providing alternative energy at low- or no-cost to underserved communities. Black Rock Solar started as a project at Burning Man to power part of Black Rock City. We\u2019re named after the Black Rock Desert in which the Burning Man event takes place, a reflection of our deep roots in the Burning Man community. The staff and board of Black Rock Solar (BRS) will be on site at the Culture Labs daily to discuss what it is that BRS does, and how to get 'plugged in' to alternative energy yourself. Consult the experts, have a glass of tea, hang out in the shade. Discover what the other Outreach groups (BRAF, Regionals, BWB) are up to. We'll have a map of Black Rock City available so you can add your camp with your alternative energy installation to it, and see what the other denizens of our fair city are up to this year."
"Barbara McArthur \"writer/editor\" - A fabulous bat!\nI had to wait until I could visit a batting cage with my 17 year-old grandson to come up with a decent review of the bat. It LOOKS lethal - or very cool. From what I experienced, and it's been a while since I've been in a batthing cage with a bat in my hand, the bat is everything they say it is - well-balanced, with the ability to flex - and the distance and speed are surely greater than I've ever accomplished with a wooden bat. My grandson echoes what I have said - and he can't wait for the snow to disappear so he can used it on the baseball team this spring. It's a real beauty in all respects!\nAfter trying many other products, Exposed Acne System has worked best! The system is easy to use and very effective. For any of you that have seen a dermotoglist, you will notice the same products recommended by your doctor are in Exposed products. I am so thankful I found this company and their products. You will be too."
"Siemens AG operates in the Turbines and turbine generator sets sector. In addition to historical fundamental analyses, the complete report available to purchase compares Siemens with three other manufacturers of engines in Europe: Vestas Wind Systems AS of Denmark (2018 sales of 75.54 billion Danish Kroner [US$11.42 billion] of which 84% was Power Solutions), Siemens Gamesa Renewable Energy SA of Spain (9.12 billion Euro [US$10.30 billion] of which 86% was Wind Turbine Manufacturing), and Alstom SA which is based in France (7.95 billion Euro [US$8.97 billion] of which 44% was Rolling stock).\nSales Analysis. Siemens reported sales of 83.04 billion Euro (US$93.73 billion) for the fiscal year ending September of 2018. This represents a decrease of 0.0% versus 2017, when the company's sales were 83.05 billion Euro. The sales level in 2018 was fairly close to the level five years ago: in 2013, Siemens had sales of 75.88 billion Euro. Contributing to the drop in overall sales was the 19.7% decline in Power and Gas, from 15.41 billion Euro to 12.38 billion Euro. There were also decreases in sales in Healthineers (down 3.1% to 13.32 billion Euro) and Reconciliation (down 14.1% to 1.09 billion Euro) . However, these declines were partially offset by the increase in sales of Digital Factory (up 14.8% to 12.23 billion Euro) and Energy Management (up 0.4% to 11.68 billion Euro) and Wind Power and Renewables (up 15.2% to 9.12 billion Euro) and Mobility (up 7.9% to 8.72 billion Euro) and Process Industries and Drives (up 0.3% to 7.22 billion Euro) and Building Technologies (up 1.9% to 6.48 billion Euro) and Financial Services (Sfs) (up 4.9% to 812.00 million Euro) ."
