Print.\nNoyes, Sybil I., Charles Thornton Libby, and Walter Goodwin Davis.Genealogical Dictionary of Maine and New Hampshire. Baltimore: Genealogical Pub., 1972. Print.\nMelick, Matthew D., Gertrude Frances. Rowell, and Valentine Rowell. A Rowell Family History: From the First Generation in America to the Pioneer Families and on toward the Present. S.l.: S.n., 2002. Print.\nAdams, Charles Thornton. The Family of James Thornton Father of Hon. Matthew Thornton. New York City: Publisher Not Identified, 1905. Print."
"Home \u00bb News \u00bb Facebook secretly sharing your data to Apple, Amazon and Microsoft?\nFacebook, perhaps the most popular social media internet site, is again under the red eye of customers for purportedly dripping their information to companies such as Apple, Microsoft, Amazon, as well as Yahoo. The record came from New York Times and stated that Facebook has been sharing data like usernames, contact details, usernames of good friends, likes, etc. without the approval of the customer.\nVisitors may be asking yourself why Facebook would do this without any advantage. However the fact is that Facebook is profiting mostly from it. They would have a lot more website traffic on their site, their customer base would raise and also the advertisements they get from their marketers would also expand in number. All this suggests an increase in revenue for Facebook. They might even market the information for financial returns from 3rd parties.\nThis is not the first time Facebook has actually been accused of selling its users\u2019 data to 3rd parties. In April, the CEO of Facebook, Mark Zuckerberg needed to encounter the Congressional hearing relating to numerous claims made by studies as well as studies on Facebook. Nonetheless, Mark rejected the claims entirely, saying \u201cWe do not market information to any individual\u201d. Whether that holds true, users, regulators, as well as media have actually taken it out on Facebook concerning privacy violations.\nAltogether, Facebook has actually turned into one of the biggest marketplaces for data on the web and the users do not also find out about it. Breaking out social media accounts, online search engine and also applications are simply \u2018information losses in disguise\u2019. All of the data that these web sites, applications, and systems accumulate are being utilized to set a target audience and also obtain advertisements.\nIn April, the CEO of Facebook, Mark Zuckerberg had to face the Legislative hearing concerning several claims made by researches and surveys on Facebook. Whether or not that is true, users, regulatory authorities, and also media have taken it out on Facebook pertaining to personal privacy breaches.\nCompletely, Facebook has actually ended up being one of the largest industries for information on the internet and the customers do not also recognize concerning it."
"M. L. Buchman raises the stakes-and the heat-in the return of the acclaimed Night Stalkers series NAME: Kara Moretti RANK: Captain of the Army stealthiest remote piloted aircraft (Don't call it a drone) MISSION: To be the eyes of the team NAME: Justin The Cowboy Roberts RANK: Captain of the Army most powerful helicopter MISSION: To redeem the past, at any cost They Put Life, Limb, and Heart on the Line. Two new captains join The Night Stalkers with two different strategies in life, love, and combat. When Brooklyn-raised Kara joins the crew, she knows one thing as an absolute truth: to stay safe, keep everything and everyone at a distance. Born in Texas, Justin knows only one honorable way to make up for losing his first crew to a suicide bomber: he flies with all his heart. When Kara and Justin collide on a top secret mission deep in the Israeli desert, then the battle truly begins."
"On damp winds they\u2019re blown in, the thunder of their blades as they slice through the air echoing over golden fields. Stalwart defenders of the nation, here they\u2019re far from war torn lands: no bombs or bullets to lay them low, only nature\u2019s unpredictable buffets to keep them humble.\nThis afternoon I was down at the wildflower meadow with my notepad and my camera when two Chinook helicopters from a local RAF airbase began circling overhead. I quickly snapped a few shots of them as they passed over, thinking they\u2019d soon be gone, only to realise that they were actually landing at the small airfield on the outskirts of the village. Now, that is not something that normally happens! I hurriedly made my way over.\nUnfortunately, I didn\u2019t actually manage to make it quite all the way to the airfield before they were taking off again, but I did manage to find a position where I could get a few decent pictures before they left. Luckily, several other villagers had also been out and about and one of them had managed to speak to one of the pilots. It seems that a bird had collided with the windscreen of one of the helicopters, forcing it to land.\nI hadn\u2019t actually planned to post today as I\u2019m still in the middle of CampNano \u2013 meaning I\u2019ve been busy editing and lengthening the flash fictions I\u2019m planning to publish as compilations on Amazon. The other photographs and poems I\u2019ve been posting lately have all ready to go since June! Another of those will probably be posted in a few days time.\nThis post is for Jacqueline\u2019s Echoes of my Neighbourhood challenge.\nexcellent Louise and all the best on Amazon!!!!\nThanks, Cybele. \ud83d\ude42 From what I\u2019ve seen helping my mum out with her books on Amazon, it\u2019s the promotion that\u2019s the hard part!\nVery cool, those Chinooks are pretty noisy aren\u2019t they?\nI\u2019ll probably put up a post about my compilation when it\u2019s ready to go, though that may still be a while off. I haven\u2019t even thought about the cover art yet!\nGreat photos! I bet that was something to see!\nThanks, PJ. \ud83d\ude42 They were very impressive. I just wish I could have got a little closer before they took off again!\nSuch cool photos! Good luck!\nThank you, Antonia. \ud83d\ude42 I\u2019m glad you like them. They were a very unexpected sight!"
"In December 1989 the average high temperature in Gulkana, AK was 20.6\u00b0F, and this was 14.7\u00b0F warmer than the average of 5.9\u00b0F. The hottest day in December 1989 was 12 December when the temperature reached 39.0\u00b0F. Overnight the average temperature in December is -10.5\u00b0F and in 1989 the average overnight temperature was 16.5\u00b0F warmer at 6.0\u00b0F.\nIn December the average monthly rainfall in Gulkana, AK is 0.50 inches with rain usually falling on 0 days. In December 1989 there was a total of 2.04 inches of rain, that fell on 2 days."
