"Whether it\u2019s Easter time or not, bunnies are a much-loved creature that we can celebrate all-year-round. From their fluffy tails to those adorably long ears, what\u2019s not to love about this animal?\nBunnies are also popularly represented in craft projects, so today we\u2019ve rounded-up 60 DIY bunny crafts ideas that rabbit lovers are going to go hopping mad for!\nIsn\u2019t this bunny plush adorable? The great news is that Alice and Lois will actually give you their free template to help you recreate your own!\nDo you know a special little one who would adore this DIY bunny bug from Alice and Lois? It\u2019s super easy to create, so you\u2019ll want to get crafting ASAP!\nThis DIY bunny ring dish is perfect for storing all of your little trinkets, plus it looks super cute too. Alice and Lois will show you how it\u2019s done!\nCan you believe that these bunnies were created from socks? You\u2019ll certainly want to check out this tutorial from A Pumpkin and a Princess to see exactly how you can make your own!\nThese homemade bath bombs are in the shape of bunnies, so they\u2019re perfect for an alternative Easter surprise or simply a gift for any occasion. A Pumpkin and a Princess is the clever blogger behind this project.\nHere\u2019s a wonderful and simple bunny craft project that your kids will love creating! Coffee Cups and Crayons has a great step-by-step tutorial that you\u2019ll want to follow.\nThis DIY burlap bunny banner is all sorts of amazing! You can simply hang one on its own, or why not create a series of the design to present as a garland? Crafts Unleashed will teach you how.\nThese DIY bunny party favors from Craft with Mum will win over any attendee! Filled with eggs, this design is also super easy to make.\nWho knew that an empty egg carton could create hours of fun? Crafty Morning will show you how to recreate this adorable bunny face. Your kids are going to love making this!\nPaint samples are widely available in paint stores, plus they\u2019re free! Collect a few and your children will love cutting out bunny shapes from the paper and turning them into this fabulous artwork, just as Crafty Morning has done.\nNow you can turn your child\u2019s hand print into a beautiful work of \u2018bunny art\u2019, thanks to this tutorial from Crafty Morning! This is one artwork you\u2019ll definitely want to display.\nThis toilet paper craft from Crafty Morning is not only pretty cute, it\u2019s also very affordable, being made from cardboard and a toilet paper roll! You\u2019ll want to thank Crafty Morning for this clever project idea.\nHere\u2019s an inexpensive craft project from Crafty Morning that you and your kids can easily whip-up within an hour! The best part? These bunnies will keep your kids entertained well beyond that.\nThese DIY bunny pouches from Craving Some Creativity are perfect for holding little Easter eggs, trinkets, or other candy \u2013 Children will adore them!\nHere\u2019s an Easter bunny surprise that you can make for your feline friend \u2013 bunny-shaped catnip pouches from Dream a Little Bigger! Make them in any color that your heart desires.\nHave you got some pine cones laying around at home or in your backyard? Fireflies and Mud Pies has this crafty idea for turning them into decorative bunnies that everyone will love!\nFive Little Chefs has something pretty special for you \u2013 a tutorial teaching you how to create your own bunny-adorned lip balm! This would make a great Easter present for those who prefer to steer clear of the chocolate.\nNovelty cushions are all the rage now, so imagine our delight at discovering these DIY bunny cushions from Go Make Me! You\u2019re sure to love this tutorial as much as we do.\nNot only are these soaps shaped as bunnies, but they also contain just 3 ingredients, including essential oils which will naturally leave your skin in its best condition. Thanks Growing Up Gabel for this awesome project!\nHappiness is Homemade has created the perfect vessel for you to store colorful Easter eggs in \u2013 these pastel jars with see-through bunny silhouettes! When it comes to Easter-themed home d\u00e9cor, does it get any better than this?\nFancy turning some old wooden spoons into these eye-catching (and adorable) bunnies, just as Hobby Craft has done? They\u2019d make excellent gifts for little loved ones, or even a special Easter surprise.\nThese pom pom bunnies from IKat Bag are so delightful, they almost look like the real thing! Children are going to love playing with these crafty creations.\nWho doesn\u2019t love donuts? Here\u2019s a DIY trick from It\u2019s Always Autumn \u2013 turn your donuts into beautiful bunnies! Check out the tutorial to see how.\nNovelty mugs are the next best thing, so why not create your own bunny version of the trend? Jewelry and Stuff has this wonderful tutorial to show you how she created this quirky mug.\nGive a boring plant pot a makeover, just as Joann has done! With bunny ears and a cute design, you can fill your pots with just about anything \u2013 from eggs to a cactus!\nThis felt bunny by Lia Griffith looks so incredibly cute, but can you believe that you can also create your own? This step-by-step guide will show you exactly how it\u2019s done!\nSpeaking of felt bunnies, here\u2019s another wonderful tutorial from Lia Griffith, this time teaching you how to make this felt bunny hair clip. Too cute!\nIt\u2019s time to embrace your inner kawaii, just as Life Ann Style has done with these DIY bunny ear scrunchies. Create them in an assortment of colors and patterns for a design that\u2019s right up your alley!\nEveryone needs a set of bunny ears, whether it\u2019s to dress up for Halloween or Easter. Life Prekarious has a simple and affordable tutorial to show you how you can recreate your own."
