"Online registration of birth certificate in UP can be done at online portal e-nagarsewaup.in. Applicants willing to apply for a birth certificate in Uttar Pradesh can visit the nearest CSC or NDMC centre for the same. Besides this, there is a facility of checking application status, verify birth certificate, and download birth certificate on the Urban Local Bodies Uttar Pradesh Website.\nAuthorized cyber cafes who have legal authority to register reported birth in UP are known as Citizen Service Centre (CSC). They are provided with all the guidelines & forms to fill the registration form as per the information provided by the applicant.\nJust visit your nearest CSC and give them details of the birth. They will fill an online registration form. Once an application is submitted, you will get an SMS on your mobile that your application for birth certificate apply has been submitted.\nThe process is simple. Visit the Nagar Nigam Service Center with all required documents. As per the details provided by you, the Nagar Nigam operator will fill the online birth registration form. Here also, you will get a confirmation message on mobile phone.\nCitizen can apply in the hospital where child is born. Here, the nurse or concerned doctors will help you fill the application form. As the child is born in their hospital, you need not to give much details. After filling the form, hospital staff will send the application form to the Urban Local Bodies for birth registration.\nYou can collect the birth certificate either from the hospital or Nagar Nigam office after passage of 21 days.\nDownload the online application form to apply for birth certificate in UP. The format of the form has been shared below. You can either fill the application form in Hindi or English Language other than these two, will not be accepted.\nTake a print out of this application form and fill it completely with required details. After filling the application form, submit it to Nagar Nigam Citizen Service Centre or the Hospital where child is born."
