"MR says: How and when you pay your tithing is a personal decision for all of us. But find out why this Church member chooses to avoid paying tithing online.\nWhat do you think about paying online tithing? Take our poll and find out more about the latest changes to tithing here.\nThe Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints has recently introduced a way to pay tithing online in some areas. I have heard different viewpoints ranging from it being more convenient and less of a hassle to not carry around a checkbook, while some have said it would cause paying tithing to become more of a bill than a personal offering to the Lord.\nI find satisfaction in paying tithing. I'm grateful that my parents taught me to never pay it grudgingly, wondering what I could have done with the extra few hundred dollars a month. I love walking up to on of the bishopric and shaking their hand and personally being accountable for the commandment.\nLead image from The 8 Ways 2."
"Five time world champion MC Mary Kom (51kg) and four time Asian Champion L Sarita Devi (60kg) reasserted their names as legends of the game by winning the championship title at the Asian women Boxing Championships in Ulaanbaatar, Mongolia on Sunday (25 March 2012). The veterans of the sport added another feather to their heavily decorated caps by winning the gold medal at sixth edition of the tournament. While Mary won her fourth gold, Sarita bagged her fifth consecutive gold medal at the continental championships. Pinky Jangra (48kg), Sonia Lather (54kg), Monica Saun (64kg) and Pooja Rani (75kg) won silver medals after losing in the finals of their respective weight categories. The Indian team will return home from the championship with 2 gold medals, 4 silver medals and 2 bronze medals ? three of those medals (two gold and one silver) coming in the Olympic weight categories. Indian finished the tournament second behind China? A monumental feat achieved by these Indian glove women, which further cements India\u2019s position as a force to be reckoned with, in the world of Women\u2019s Boxing.\nShri Abhay Singh Chautala, the President of the Indian Amateur Boxing Federation has applauded the excellent performance of the Indian team at the 6th Asian Women\u2019s Boxing Championship and said it was a well deserved accomplishment.\nIn his message Mr. Chautala stated,?\u201cIndian women have always done exceptionally well at the Continental Championships; this year our boxers have once again displayed outstanding talent and spirit to win the runner\u2019s up trophy. MC Mary Kom and Sarita Devi have been the pioneers of the sport in the country. What they have accomplished is beyond comparison and makes them the true hero\u2019s of the sport\u201d.?He further added,?\u201cThis performance will do wonders for the Indian team\u2019s confidence and we positively believe the Indian women pugilists will performance as well in the Olympic Qualifying tournament, the World Championships in May\u201d."
