"We have clinics across the whole of North Yorkshire and York which offer a range of sexual health and contraception services. This means you will be able to access all of your sexual health care provided in one place at one time. This includes tests and treatments for sexually transmitted infections (STIs) and HIV, a range of contraception options, free condoms and advice.\nOur Community Outreach Team Yorkshire MESMAC, one of the largest sexual health organisations in the country, offer free and confidential rapid HIV tests outside of clinic locations, as well as free condoms, counselling and support.\nOur Positive Support Team North Yorkshire AIDS Action (NYAA) is here to support you, if you or someone you care for, has been diagnosed with HIV. NYAA is an established charity that provides practical and emotional support to people living with or affected by HIV.\nIf you can't find what you're looking for, please call our central booking and information line on 01904 721111 (open from 9am until 5pm, Monday to Thursday & Friday 9am - 4pm) where our staff will be able to help or simply fill in our contact us form and we will get back in touch. Your GP can also offer you a range of free and confidential sexual health care."
"Ispahani Islamia Eye Institute and Hospital began as a charitable dispensary founded by Mr. M. A. Ispahani, an industrialist and philanthropist. It developed into a pioneering eye hospital in 1960, providing basic ophthalmic services, as well as various tertiary ophthalmic specialties.\nIslamia Eye Hospital, located in Dhaka, is the largest multispecialty eye hospital in Bangladesh. At Islamia, they place an emphasis on quality eye care for all socioeconomic sections of society. Early in its existence, the eye hospital began providing training to increase the human resource capacity for ophthalmic services in Bangladesh. From this concept, the M. A. Ispahani Institute of Ophthalmology was established as a sister organization in 1992 to teach advanced ophthalmology to surgeons, as well as to paramedics and nurses. Over the years, Islamia has established itself as a leading ophthalmic organization in Bangladesh for providing specialized services and training courses.\nSeva has supported Islamia since 2005 through funding the training of hospital staff as well as providing subsidies for free and low-cost service delivery through the TOMS One for One Program, as well as Focusing Philanthropy\u2019s World Sight Day campaigns."
