ending on their experience and goals as a pilot. Our mountain flying season lasts from September through the end of May. These months are great for flying at both our flight park, and soaring in our local mountains working on improving our thrermaling and cross country skills and knowledge. Our ability to be many places at once with our high caliber staff is unmatched as is our presence in our community support all pilots.\nNumerous pilots have taken advantage of the \u201cEagle For Life\u201d program. Those who know they will be spending at least a week a year in Santa Barbara, and have spent time working with our team see the enormous value in this program. We are available to instruct and guide pilots in this program anytime we are teaching at Elings Flight Park or guiding in our local mountains. There aren\u2019t many flyable days at either these locations where the Eagle team is missing from the action. Our local presence is obvious when following the dialogue on the Santa Barbara flying communities chat box discussion. The Eagle team is always in action flying with our students and supporting our local flying community like nobody else.\nPilots wanting their P3 certification can schedule a training with Eagle in order to have us to make an evaluation, and help you achieve the P3 rating. We review your log book, the glider models you have flown, and go over the requirements checklist together. We work to build your knowledge and skill set, and discuss your flying goals. This perspective and view allows us to get a vision of where you see yourself as a pilot in the future, and develop specific goals to get you there. Pilots who spend time with our team in any of our continuing education offerings usually end up joining us at our Paragliding Tours and Paragliding Clinics.\nText \u2013 Pilots wanting their P4 certification can schedule a training with Eagle in order to have us to make an evaluation, and help you achieve the P4 rating. We review your log book, the 