"The movie Clash of the Titans 2 aka Wrath of the Titans: trailer, clips, photos, soundtrack, news and much more!\nWhen the Titan king will rise the world will end! Well unless Perseus (Sam Worthington) saves the day!\nThe cyclops are a breed of one-eyed cannibal giants endowed with brute strength.\nThe Minotaur is a ferocious combination of man and bull. He is an unholy union of brutality and terror! The only thing more fearsome than his power is his rage!\nWrath of the Titans \u2013 Gods don\u2019t die.\nWrath of the Titans \u2013 Being half human makes you stronger than a god, not weaker.\nWrath of the Titans \u2013 We are brothers.\nWrath of the Titans \u2013 What are you waiting for?\nThe sequel to Clash of the Titans is directed by Jonathan Liebesman.\nThose Siamese monsters are fearsome fighters!\nWrath of the Titans \u2013 Yes, but on my terms.\nThe half-god Perseus (Sam Worthington) has to rescue his daddy, Zeus (Liam Neeson), in this sequel to Clash of the Titans.\nI really wish I had a chimera for loyal pet! Then thieves, and my mother in law, would stay clear from my home for sure!\nThe poster above features Actor Edgar Ramirez as Ares, the Greek god of war.\nIn theaters: March 30, 2012.\nSam Worthington really needs a haircut!\nFeel the wrath of the Titans at your local theaters on March 30, 2012.\nThe film is directed by Jonathan Liebesman. It will hit theaters on March 30, 2012.\nWrath of the Titans will hit theaters on March 30, 2012.\n\u201cA decade after his heroic defeat of the monstrous Kraken, Perseus\u2014the demigod son of Zeus\u2014is attempting to live a quieter life as a village fisherman and the sole parent to his 10-year old son, Helius. Meanwhile, a struggle for supremacy rages between the gods and the Titans. Dangerously weakened by humanity\u2019s lack of devotion, the gods are losing control of the imprisoned Titans and their ferocious leader, Kronos, father of the long-ruling brothers Zeus, Hades and Poseidon. The triumvirate had overthrown their powerful father long ago, leaving him to rot in the gloomy abyss of Tartarus, a dungeon that lies deep within the cavernous underworld.\nThe sequel will be directed by Jonathan Liebesman.\nDirector Jonathan Liebesman (who helmed the Killing Room and Battle Los Angeles) has been hired by Warner Bros to helm the movie sequel to Clash of the Titans.\nThe plot of Clash of the Titans 2 hasn\u2019t been announced yet, but Sam Worthington and Gemma Arterton will most likely reprise their roles as Perseus and Io in the movie Clash of the Titans 2.\nI wonder if Sam Worthington will still be at the center of this movie sequel to Clash of the Titans. But knowing how the studios, I guess they\u2019d rather have the same lead character. So I suppose Sam Worthington will reprise his role as Perseus in the movie Clash of the Titans 2."
