"It doesn\u2019t matter where you go, a locals restaurant or a touristic one, you will always find on your table a sometimes red, sometimes yellow creamy paste called AJI that can be confused with ketchup \u2026. be careful! is usually very hot and DELICIOUS, and WE can\u2019t imagine our life without it.\nGoing back to the chili paste, we put it in almost everything: soups, entrees, main courses\u2026 there is also a variety of Pisco sour made of\u2026 Yes, CHILI.\nLocals say, for example, that a good Ceviche is that one that makes you cry, and not necessarily of pleasure\u2026 one thing we like is the sensation of a cold beer refreshing your palate after such intakes of AJI paste. Wondering when this hot tradition started? back in the Prehispanic times, Incas and Pre-Inca cultures loved chili: no refrigerators available made this product a good way to increase or dissimulate certain undesired flavors, another great reason is that this product is a great bactericide, they possibly got to understand that by eating it and feeling less incidence of stomach ache and started to use it regularly since then, today\u2019s people of the most remote communities of this nation still use this natural remedy as a great condiment to their food.\nIf you want my advice: try it but in moderation\u2026 a tiny spoon first and the more if your tongue can resist it.\nP.s. Get first a big glass of water and make sure is right next to you, just in case.\nThanks a lot for liking our posts, I hope you are enjoying the content already. Best regards!"
"Continuing from where we left off in 7 Steps to Take after Motor Vehicle Accidents (Pt. 1), here, we will resume our discussion of what to do after motor vehicle accidents in order to preserve what rights you may have to compensation.\nStep 3 \u2013 Exchange driving info with the other involved motorists.\nExchanging information with other motorists is one of the essential steps to take after motor vehicle accidents. Another critical step is calling us for help getting the compensation you may deserve.\nInsurance providers and policy numbers.\nConsider getting the names and contact info for any witnesses to the accident.\nAs you take down this info, consider using your cellphone or other mobile device so that you can text and/or email all of the info to yourself.\nIf you do end up using your cell phone or mobile device and the device has a camera, consider taking a picture of each involved motorists\u2019 driver\u2019s license to facilitate the exchange of info.\nStep 4 \u2013 Take pictures of the damage caused by the accident.\nSnap photos of all of the damage to your vehicle, including any obvious dents, broken windows/mirrors, etc.\nTake pictures of the other vehicles involved in the accident.\nTake pictures of any immobile objects that may have been hit by the vehicles in the collision.\nSnap photos of any visible injuries you and/or any passengers in your vehicle may have sustained in the accident.\nAs with the information you collect from other drivers, using your cell phone to take these photos \u2013 and then to text or email them to yourself \u2013 is a smart idea, as many of these mobile devices are equipped with good cameras and having copies of these photos in your text or email inbox can allow you to easily send them out to others who may need them in the future (like, for instance, an attorney or your insurance provider).\nWe will wrap up our discussion of what to do after motor vehicle accidents in the upcoming conclusion to this blog series \u2013 be sure you look for it!\nSchedule a free initial consultation with us by calling (719) 635-5886 or (800) 383-5886. You can also email us using the contact form on this page. We don\u2019t get paid unless or until you get paid, so you have nothing to lose and everything to gain by contacting us today."
