f dishes.\nOur truffle products are made from our freshly harvested Tasmanian truffles harvested through the winter months.\nThe products contains locally produced Tasmanian truffles with no added artificial aromas.\nThe Truffle Salt is produced from freshly harvested Tasmanian truffles and Tasman Sea salt flakes.\nTruffle salt is a simple way to enjoy truffles. Try it with cooked egg dishes, tossed in pasta, on p\u00e2t\u00e9, or simply use to season meat dishes and vegetables.\nAll our truffle products are made from our freshly harvested French black truffles harvested through the winter months.\nThe Truffle Savoury Gift Selection includes truffle mustard, truffle salt, truffle oil and the truffle mushroom tapenade.\nThe selection includes a combination of truffle mustard, truffle salt and truffle oil.\nThe truffle mustard is very versatile the only limitation is your imagination. A perfect condiment for a wide range of dishes.\nTruffle salt is a simple way to enjoy truffles. It adds flavour and aroma to a number of dishes particularly good on grilled meats and roasted potatoes, ideal on scrambled eggs and even popcorn with a good butter.\nThe truffle oil is a gourmet delicacy to delight your taste buds, perfect with pasta, risotto, eggs, potatoes and right through to soups and as part of a dressing on salads.\nTake the heady aromas of White Truffle fused with the earthy richness of Black Truffle and you have a sensational taste capturing the best of both worlds.\nUsing the best traditional and cutting edge methods with rich Australian olive oil, we have an amazing gourmet delicacy. Try our truffle oil with pasta, risotto, eggs or potatoes and right through to soups and salads.\nCombination of the Tasmanian truffle salt and the Tasmanian Truffle Mushroom Tapenade.\nThe Perigord Truffle hamper is a selection of truffle products made from freshly harvested truffles.\nThe selection includes truffle salt, truffle honey, truffle honey with hazelnuts, truffle honey with macadamia nuts and truffle oil.\nThe truffle honey is a perfect pairing for good strong cheeses such as blue cheeses and cheddars. The truffle honey adds sweetness and the nuances of the truffle also compliments marinades in poultry dishes.\nThe truffle honey with hazelnuts and truffle honey with macadamia nuts are ideal as a desert served with ice cream or simply stirred into yoghurt.\nThe products contain locally produced Australian French truffles with no added artificial aromas.\nTasmanian truffles infused into a mild golden amber honey.\nThe sweet, fragrant honey is laced with chopped black truffle, creating a balance of earthiness and sweetness that explodes in your mouth with flavour.\nThe truffle honey adds sweetness and the nuances of the truffle, complements marinades for poultry dishes and can be drizzled over cheese or served with steamed vegetables.\nAll our truffle products are made from our freshly harvested Tasmanian black truffles harvested through the winter months.\nThe product contain locally produced Tasmanian truffles with no added artificial aromas.\nA honey with freshly harvested Tasmanian truffles and hazelnuts.\nThe flavour of the truffles adds to the sweetness of the honey and the nuttiness of the hazelnut. Adds flavour and texture to vegetable dishes. In deserts pour over ice cream or simply stir into yoghurt.\nThe product contains locally produced Australian French truffles with no added artificial aromas.\nThe new truffle hamper selection includes truffle mustard, truffle salt, truffle oil, truffle dressing and truffle honey.\nThe truffle dressing is the perfect addition to a salad, flavouring pasta dishes or just dipping with bread.\nA honey with freshly harvested Tasmanian truffles and macadamia nuts.\nThe flavour of the truffles complements the honey and the smoothness of the macadamia nuts. In desserts pour over ice cream or simply stir into yoghurt. Very enjoyable with ice cream and other dairy products or simply served with a dessert wine after dinner.\nThe product contains locally produced Tasmanian truffles with no added artificial aromas.\n\u00a9 2019 Perigord Truffles of Tasmania."
