"Welcome to Jakarta, the capital of Indonesia. With a population of some 10 million, this frenzied city with its humid sprawl and contrasting vast air-conditioned shopping malls is a fantastic example of East meeting West.\nThis vibrant city has changed dramatically within the last few years and in many areas meets the standards of other international cities, but some of the infrastructure and road systems leave it firmly in the past.\nThe traffic congestion is a constant conversation topic, as well as the fact that it is a superb hub to explore Asia from. Love or hate it, it continues to be one of the well populated locations for expats of all nationalities and backgrounds."
"In this post, I lay out some general tips on how to begin searching for records to sample for making hip-hop beats.\nIs a Degree in Audio Production or Music Business Worth It?\nI often hear a question along the lines of, \u201cIs it worth going to college to land a career in the music industry?\u201d The question is complicated to answer, but I have plenty of advice to offer to those of you who are considering a career in music.\nLearn the basics of recording, editing, and chopping music samples for beat production.\nSo you want to assemble a home recording rig? Whether you want to explore a new hobby or establish a budding career in audio production, I want to help you seek out the necessary equipment. I will also point out what you don\u2019t need, as well as dispel some misconceptions and common pitfalls."
