"Just last week we got the confirmation that Borderlands 2 is in the making. (yay!) This week get got some details of some of the new improvements and changes via the latest copy of Game Informer.\n-Bearded drawf guy is Salvador, the Gunzerker. Special ability is Dual-wielding. Any weapon can be dual-wield.\n-The original Vault Hunters will be support NPC\u2019s.\n-Bandits now have their own brand of weaponry.\n-Weapons can have custom decals and enhancements.\n-Enemies are more responsive, and actually interact with each other better.\n-The players will also have interacting dialogues, similar to those in Left 4 Dead.\n-BL2\u2019s skill tree will maintain the 3 Branch system and have more defined abilities rather than simple stat boosts. It is unknown how many skills will occupy each branch.\n-2 Gunzerker Skills were mentioned. One, increases the fire rate of any weapon the longer the trigger is held down. A second, while Dual-wielding, increases accuracy with same class weapons, or doubles damage for different class weapons.\nThat\u2019s a whole lot of awesome right there."
"Or you can simply step foot inside the shower, which is just as effective for dealing with anxiety yet without those really unfavorable side effects associated with the intake of sedatives.\nContinue reading if you want to learn about some of the best ways to use your shower for immediate attainment of relief of anxiety \u2014 below you will come across a few very simply yet highly effective ones.\nMost of the time, an anxiety attack tends to strike each time you are mentally and physically stressed. And when you are stressed, your muscles tend to tense up.\nDo take note that your anxiety can cause your muscles to tighten even more. Clearly, anxiety and stress can feed each other, thus creating a self-perpetuating problem.\nThis is why it\u2019s a great idea for you to have a warm shower as soon as you feel stressed or anxious \u2014 warm water is very good at loosening those tight muscles.\nIt\u2019s no secret that an anxiety attack can leave you feeling exhausted, which is something that can keep you from carrying out the rest of your everyday duties and responsibilities.\nTaking a cold shower is highly recommended if what you need is a dose of mental alertness. Experts say that it can also encourage production of more happy hormones.\nA lot of people swear by the anxiety-busting properties of taking a warm shower first and then ending it with a cold shower for a couple of minutes.\nDon\u2019t just arm yourself with a bottle of shower gel and loofah \u2014 playing music in the background can also help make an anxiety attack go away so much faster.\nFor many people, listening to relaxing instrumental tracks such as those that you often hear being played at day spas is great for eliminating their anxiety. For others, songs that boast of upbeat tempos work so much better.\nSince the bathroom offers nice acoustics, why not sing , too? Experts say that singing can actually encourage production of happy hormones vital for having your mood lifted.\nIn the world of aromatherapy, certain essential oils are known to be perfect for people who suffer from stress and anxiety and want to attain all-natural relief from those.\nJasmine, chamomile, lavender, valerian, bergamot, holy basil, frankincense, ylang ylang, rose, lemon balm, orange, marjoram, geranium, patchouli \u2014 there are lots of stress- and anxiety-busting essential oils to choose from!\nWhat you need to do is place a few drops of your chosen essential oil on a cotton ball and leave it in the shower a few minutes before you actually take a shower.\nSometimes there\u2019s no need for you to get your hands on a bottle of essential oil with known calming and soothing properties for the sake of beating anxiety.\nIt\u2019s also possible for you to turn every shower time into an anxiety-relieving pursuit simply by investing in some shower essentials with fantastic smells like lavender or jasmine.\nHowever, just make sure that you opt for something that contains natural fragrances \u2014 artificial fragrances can cause hormonal disruption which is something that can in fact wreak havoc on your mental health.\nGot family members and friends who have anxiety attacks every now and then, too? Then don\u2019t forget to repost this article before you go so that they may also give the above tips a try.\nWARNING: If you tend to have anxiety attacks all the time and you already find it hard to have a normal day, it\u2019s a good idea for you to seek the help of a mental health professional."
"European Space Agency astronaut Matthias Maurer is learning Chinese in preparation for a potential trip to the future Chinese Space Station, and looking forward to eating Chinese food in space.\nESA regularly sends astronauts to the International Space Station, but the lack of launch capability means taking a ride with other space-faring nations, and in the future that could include China.\n\"Europe has no proper capsule to fly to space so we always need to have a rocket and to be invited by another nation. Currently we fly on a Soyuz rocket, so everyone who flies on a Soyuz rocket needs to learn Russian,\" Maurer said in an ESA WebTV interview at the Berlin Air and Space Show on April 27.\n\"In the future we might fly to the new Chinese Space Station, and of course, if you want to fly with the Chinese you need to learn Chinese.\"\nAsked by interviewer Kelsea Brennan-Wessels if he likes Chinese food, Maurer replied: \"It&apos;s brilliant, so I would love to have Chinese food in space\".\nIn August 2017, Maurer and ESA colleague Sam Cristoforetti travelled to China for joint sea survival training off the coast of Shandong Province.\nThe exercises were part of growing cooperation between the China Manned Space Engineering Office (CMSE) and ESA in human spaceflight that could one day see Europeans fly with Chinese to the Chinese Space Station.\nMaurer is also a part of Spaceship EAC, a programme in which students and scientists work together to tackle future space exploration challenges. The initiative, which he also introduces in the interview, includes preparing astronauts and technology for missions to the Moon.\nHe is close to finishing basic and pre-assignment training, and waiting for a mission to the International Space Station.\nConstruction of China&apos;s space station is expected to start around 2020 with the launch of the Tianhe core module and be completed by around 2022 with the addition of two further 20 metric tonne experiment modules, Wentian and Mengtian."
