or about 2 hours without issues. he only bug I saw remained is in that in some conversations a few words are cut-off. For the rest it runs like a dream in my tests on my Nvidia 640M iMac.\nThe Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim Wrapper update!\nOn November 14, 2014 / Gamersgate Games, Mac RPG Games, Video Tutorial, Wrapper updates / Comments Off on The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim Wrapper update!\nHere a video and Wrapper update of Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim! The game was \u201cglitchy\u201d in the past, but with the latest Wrapper the game is \u201cplayable\u201d again in lowest settings. The video below shows the game-play a bit when you have a 512mb Nvidia GFX card iMac (which I have). Hope you enjoy the new Steam Wrapper."
"How to use Zapya on iOS \u2013 Enjoy Zapya!\nBefore opening Zapya, make sure that both mobile devices are connected to the same Wi-Fi hotspot or network. Open the Android app and select Connect to Other Device, then select Connect to iOS. Open the settings on the iOS device and click the Wi-Fi button, then search for the Wi-Fi name that appears on the Android device. Once found, click on that Wi-Fi and connect to it. Both devices should now be connected. When Upon connecting to the Android device, the main screen should reappear and now you can freely transfer files of any kind to the Android device.\nBefore opening the app, make sure that both mobile devices are connected to the same Wi-Fi hotspot or network. Open the application on the iOS device and click the \u201cConnect to Friends\u201d button. A window will pop up on your phone with a list of all of the other devices connected to the same Wi-Fi as yours. Find the name of the Mac and click on it to connect. Upon connecting to the Mac, the main screen should reappear and now you can freely transfer files of any kind to the Mac.\nOpen up Zapya on the PC first that you can find the PC\u2019s username and password. Once you have located the username and password of the PC, go to your iOS device\u2019s Settings. Go to \u201cWi-Fi\u201d and sign into the Wi-Fi network that matches the username of the PC. Upon connecting to the PC\u2019s network, open up Zapya on your iOS device. Since you are connected to the PC\u2019s network, the PC\u2019s icon will be located on the top of the main screen already when you open Zapya. Now you can freely transfer files of any kind to the PC.\nIf the PC is connected to more than one device, upon selecting a file to transfer a window will appear. The window will give you the option of which device(s) you wish to transfer the file to. Once you have selected the device(s) you want to transfer the file to, click \u201cOK\u201d and the file will transfer automatically."
"A 2016 survey showed that the poll worker shortage faced by local elections officials has gotten worse, while current workers skew older. How can jurisdictions hire younger people to sign up for these gigs?\nIn Montana, many voters, including Native Americans, rely on volunteers to collect and deliver their absentee ballots. But a referendum next month would end the practice.\nRegistering voters in a majority Native American county.\nIn November, voters in Colorado, Michigan, Missouri and Utah will decide whether independent commissioners instead of state lawmakers should draw draw congressional and state legislative maps.\nNearly a thousand polling places have been closed in the five years since the U.S. Supreme Court struck down key parts of the Voting Rights Act.\nThe confusion in June primary elections in Maryland and California\u2014caused by computer glitches and human error\u2014show what could happen if foreign adversaries successfully hack voter registration information, experts say.\nThis was a year of unparalleled success for the gun-control movement in the United States.\nMore than 20 states allow mobile polling, which involves bipartisan pairs of election officials bringing ballots directly to long-term care facilities for the elderly.\nOther states could follow Maine into ranked-choice voting, currently used in 11 cities across the country.\nSo States Ban Bump Stocks. Now How Do They Enforce the Law?\nNew Jersey is not the only state having trouble enforcing its ban. In Massachusetts, where residents had until February to surrender their bump stocks, State Police received just three devices.\nSo-called permitless carry laws now are in effect in more than 10 states.\nElection officials have figured out how to keep voting lines down, but communities of color are still waiting longer to vote.\nFor years, advocates have called victims of domestic violence part of the country\u2019s \u201chidden homeless.\u201d But now, for the first time, they\u2019re being included in the national homelessness count.\nState officials can continue using the controversial power, a federal court rules."
