"A bumper weekend of Easter racing action at the Adrian Flux Arena kicks off on Saturday 20th April 5:30pm with a fans favourite line-up. Unlimited Bangers racing in their East Anglian Championship and will be joined by Two Litre Saloon Stock Cars and 1300cc Stock Cars.\nThe spectator gates will open at 3:30pm. The arena boasts great viewing all around (plenty of under-cover viewing too!), FREE on site and overflow parking, disabled viewing, licensed bars, ample food outlets and other great facilities.\nThere are currently 86 Unlimited Bangers, 38 2L Stock Cars & 43 1300cc Stock Cars booked in to race.\nThis meeting is fully booked - If you are booked in and are no longer able to race please let us know asap as we have reserves who are unable to get a booking. If you do are not booked in and would like to be added to the reserve list please text 07939 580652. Please note if you do not get a booking please do not turn up as you will not be allowed to race.\nThe Unlimited Bangerss make their first appearance at the track since the Icebreaker event in January, with the East Anglian Championship on offer, one of the oldest and most prestigious titles at King\u2019s Lynn. Defending East Anglian Champions Shayne Winsor (160) is not scheduled, so a new name from the star studded line-up looks likely to be added to the trophy this year.\nDo you want to be the headline sponsor - you could be for just \u00a320 - visit this link here to find out how you could win that chance.\nTwo litre World Champion Lee Clarke (247) and Under 25 Champion Callum Gill (757) - both former winners of the title will lead the charge. They will be joined by other former winners including Danny Sutton (439) and a welcome visit from Mark Whittaker (67) who makes a rare banger outing.\nFormer World of Shale champion Dave Vincent (22), National points champion Lee White (830) and former World Champions Davey Cox (119) and Darren Fendley (673) are further big names in a heavyweight line-up.\nBilly Smith (161) also joining us following his outing at the MK1 Almera/ All Sunny meeting two weeks ago, where as you would expect; he was fully involved.\nThose more likely to be looking for a big crash include regular visitors Team Sowter/Filmer, made up of Carl (288) and Taylor Sowter (388), plus Jack (883) and Tom (884) Filmer. Taylor in particular will be looking to stay at the top of the Entertainers league.\nDrivers from far afield are looking to join us, including the Devon duo Buddy (262) and Jonny (362) James, or closer to home with the local Predator representatives; and overseas long distance traveller Dutchman Dennis Vorkink (211) all of which middle of the action.\nOthers to keep an eye on include James Licquorice (51) making a rare Unlimited Banger outing. Scott Gough (99), Aston Burt (246) and Brett Jackson (551) all who like to gat stuck in too!\nDon't expect 246 Aston Burt to be taking home a straight car!\nWith a number of representatives from the entertaining Gladiators, Mad Hatters, Predators and The Aftermath teams, this meeting is going to be a good one!\nThe Saloons are a fans favourite and it\u2019s not hard to work out why - hard impact, no holds barred Stock Car racing \u2013 sit back and listen to the arena fill with the sound of clashing metal. As you would expect the 2 Litre Saloon Stock Cars have once again been in top form around the King\u2019s Lynn oval this year with more the same expected Saturday 20th!\n2L Stock Cars - where action is the attraction!\nLast time here it was a night for the lower graders with each race being won by a White or Yellow grader. Trent Arthurton (610) took the win in the meeting final last time out, no mean feat with a field of top drivers chasing you down.\nRyan Santry (389) took a heat win last time out, the on board video recorder he had fixed last time, made for interesting viewing \u2013 he sure did get stuck in and likely to again this time!\nJoining us from Scotland is Barry Russell (600), who loves his shale racing and very rarely misses a meeting with us; he will be joined by no less than four other fellow Scots; Euan Mathieson (125), Aaryn Triggs (620), Graeme Shevill (661) and Alan Ainslie (777).\nAction is guaranteed whenever 26 Tommy Barnes is on track!\nShane Emerson (888) will lead the charge in the 25 and Under Championship he will have his work cut out with some big, big names looking to take the trophy from him.\nThe entry list joining us is really a who\u2019s who of the 1300 scene; with a lot of the top drivers coming to King\u2019s Lynn to be with us. World of Shale Champion and Points champion Dan Booth (216) will be leading the line-up; the defence of his silver roof points title didn\u2019t get off to the best start, but he will be surely one to watch this weekend.\nJacob Bromley (303) currently leads the National Points, but had a disappointing night here last time 16th March, he will bounce back in form almost certainly.\nBarry Wade (731) follows behind Bromley in second spot in the points chart following a great start to the year and he will be looking to continue that run of form.\nAlso finding some good results early in the season were the likes of Todd Payne (149), Startrax National Points champion Tom Keep (367), Kevin Shinn (400) and Chris Taylor (421), who will all be looking to continue. This group is not to be messed with either and know what the front bumper is for.\nJack Lower (142) and Ben Englestone (769) have been the final winners so far this year at our two orevious meetings; will there be a different final winner this time?\nAll the fun of the fair will be at King's Lynn on Saturday. The good news for mum and dad is that the ride will be free for the kids to go on as often as they like! Once we have confirmation of what ride will be with us on Saturday we will publish details of it here!"
"Spending holidays without having to spend a lot of money? Of course you can! Just go to Taman Kunci di Kota Tangerang! Taman Kunci? Yes, Taman Kunci is an abbreviation of Kupu-kupu and Kelinci (butterflies and rabbits). This park is part of a thematic park program promoted by the Tangerang City administration.\nOf the many parks in the Tangerang, Taman Kunci is one of the interesting educational tourist destinations. This park is located on Jalan Thamrin, Cikokol, Tangerang and opposite to Taman Potret. This 8000 m2 park offers a beautiful atmosphere with shady trees and several seats for visitors who want to relax. Taman Kunci makes the atmosphere in the heart of Tangerang a little greener.\nAs the name implies, this park is also a place for inspection and supervision of butterflies and rabbits. You can see through the park administrators effort who make a barrier for visitors who want to see the animals, so visitors can\u2019t interact directly. Visitors can only look from outside the enclosure, to avoid unwanted things. At the beginning of the Taman Kunci opening, visitors are allowed to play with rabbits that are released around the park on purpose. Although it seems more natural, but the safety and health of rabbits is less guaranteed.\nPark rangers always check rabbits health regularly every two weeks. So, if there are sick rabbits, they will immediately be separated and quarantined until they are healthy again. At Taman Kunci, rabbits are also fed regularly, use rabbit pellets, carrots, kale, grass, and other vegetables.\nAside rabbits, there is also butterflies that are left to live freely in a unique dome-shaped building that stands in the middle of the park. Butterflies with beautiful colors immediately welcoming you as soon as they enter this dome.\nTaman Kunci can be an alternative destination that is not only cheap, but also educating. Perfect for spending your weekend with your family!"
"By blurring the line between digital information and physical settings, augmented reality is helping construction teams become more efficient.\nYou should never give a knife and fork to a potato.\nInfographic: What are the top weapons in science fiction?\nThe following infographic provided by Sci-Fi Weapons shows the most powerful and top weapons in science fiction.\nGalactus has always been one of my favorite Marvel characters and should really have his own movie.\nIt\u2019s easy to assume that all movies about learning and education follow the same plot arc.\nInfographic: Are seniors as crazy for the internet as the younger generation?\nThe most significant reason for seniors going online is to stay in touch with family and friends through email or social networks.\nOver time, even the smallest annoyances about our personal spaces can build up, raising the levels of stress hormones in our bodies.\nIf every suitable home rooftop in the United States installed solar panels, 75% of all residential energy could come from renewable sources.\nSo what can companies do to provide a great customer experience but still take steps to avoid exposing customer data?\nThe Galaxy S's AMOLED and Super AMOLED displays have always been among the very best on smartphones.\nInfographic: Can AI replace your manager?\nSometimes it is helpful to outsource these tasks to managers, accountants, payroll services, and more.\nAmericans spend around eight hours per weekday at the office with our pets anxiously awaiting our return.\nThough there is still much to learn about this seasonal condition, proven treatments in the form of light therapies exist.\nInfographic: How long does it take to rank in Google?\nThis infographic provided by The Website Group will give you an idea how long it takes to rank in Google.\nThe newest wearables can tell us our heartbeats and our VO max numbers.\nSmart home products and appliances will be much easier to find in stores as the years go on.\nInfographic: Are self-driving cars our future?\nThere is no easy answer to that question as there is a myriad of factors that go into it.\nInfographic: Is artificial intelligence good or evil?\nToday, China is home to an estimated 200 million surveillance cameras, about four times as many as in the United States.\nYou start to ask yourself how sitting in front of a computer all day can make you so tired.\nInfographic: When was the last time you Googled yourself?\nOur searchable information, even as basic as our first and last name, is perhaps more identifiable than we may realize.\nAn automated workforce makes for some incredibly streamlined operations.\nTheir first product was the Apple I, a personal computer designed and hand-built by Wozniak."
